--- !u!114 &4849798537957608515
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 6987790286221488165}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 12f04173bf60f29418d34b4a6e743a68, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  factText: {fileID: 5577945338913254950}
  facts:
  - In medieval Europe, "witches" were often just women who knew too much about herbs.
  - "The infamous Witch Trials once used a \"swimming test\": if you floated, you
    were a witch. If you sank\u2026 sorry."
  - "The word \"witch\" comes from the Old English wicce, meaning \u201Cwise woman.\u201D"
  - "Broomsticks became associated with witches thanks to old folk rituals involving\u2026
    flying ointments. (Don\u2019t ask.)"
  - "In some legends, witches kept \"familiars\"\u2014spirit animals like cats, toads,
    or suspiciously chatty crows."
  - Not all witches were feared, many villages had a local witch people went to for
    love spells or a cure for warts.
  - "Salem wasn\u2019t the only place with witch hunts, Germany, Scotland, and France
    were way worse."
  - "\u201CWitch bottles\u201D were buried under homes in old England to ward off
    curses. Contents included nails, hair, and sometimes... urine."
  - Modern witchcraft (Wicca) is recognized as a real religion in several countries.
  - "During the witch hunts, \u201Cevidence\u201D included dreams, birthmarks, or
    owning a black cat. Justice was\u2026 creative."
  - "Confessing to witchcraft didn\u2019t save you. Denying it didn\u2019t help either.
    Lose-lose."
  - "Witches weren\u2019t always women, plenty of men got accused too. #Equality\u2026
    kind of?"
  - "Some trials involved pricking the accused with needles to find a \u201Cwitch\u2019s
    mark.\u201D If it didn\u2019t hurt, guilty."
  - You could be accused of witchcraft just for being disliked. Medieval drama was
    brutal.
  - "Witch hunters sometimes charged fees for their \u201Cservices.\u201D Business
    was booming."
  - "Being too old, too young, too pretty, too strange, any of it could get you burned\u2026
    #StayAverage"
  - In parts of Europe, accused witches were burned at the stake, not for magic,
    but for heresy. #HarshVibes.
  interval: 8
